macho_alias_names_arm64 -- arm64 Mach-O dylib with several nlist names at one
function entry.

What it is
  A 17,104-byte MH_DYLIB, SHA-256
  73f4735a6879b7f9b71d6b9ba2d4b5831b54a57234c8ad556ea4140de8b73855, linked
  from macho_alias_names.s (GH #1357's assembly plus one block) and
  macho_alias_names_other.s:
    0x240 _audit_export_a, _audit_export_b   (both external, both exported)
    0x248 _audit_local_a, _audit_local_b     (local)
    0x250 _audit_caller                      (external, `b _audit_local_a`)
    0x254 _audit_first, _audit_shared, _audit_both   (local, first object)
    0x25c _audit_shared                      (local, second object)
    0x264 _audit_second, _audit_both         (local, second object)
  nlist order puts each object's locals in definition order, then the
  externals, so the first name listed at each address is the reported one.

How it was built (no macOS SDK; host clang + the rustup-bundled ld64.lld)
  clang -target arm64-apple-macos11 -c macho_alias_names.s -o a.o
  clang -target arm64-apple-macos11 -c macho_alias_names_other.s -o b.o
  LLD=$(rustc --print sysroot)/lib/rustlib/$(rustc -vV | sed -n 's/host: //p')/bin/gcc-ld/ld64.lld
  "$LLD" -arch arm64 -dylib -platform_version macos 11.0 11.0 -fixup_chains \
         -install_name @rpath/libalias.dylib -o macho_alias_names_arm64 a.o b.o
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0-1ubuntu1.1, LLD 20.1.8 (rustc 1.90.0). Prebuilt because CI
  has no Mach-O linker.

What it pins
  One inventory row per address, the second names kept as aliases; decompile by
  any of them, in either spelling, selects that entry. `_audit_shared` (and
  `audit_shared`) selects 0x25c, the function of that name, over 0x254's alias;
  `_audit_both` is an alias at two addresses and is reported ambiguous.
